## WASHING PROCEDURE

### TO WASH

1. Before starting washing, check the following: Connect the water supply hose and open the water tap.
- Lay the drain hose down toward a sinkhole. (In case no drain pump)
- Place the drain hose in sink or bath. (In case drain pump)
- Connect the power cord to the power supply outlet.
2. Set the WASH SELECTOR KNOB to the desired mode.<PIC:Manual39_4>
{{image description: Wash Selector control drawing with Soft and Normal positions, showing the knob or slider set between the two labels.}}


3. Set the WATER SELECTOR KNOB to WASH. FOR B TYPE <PIC:Manual39_5>
{{image description: Water selector diagram with labels wash and spin, showing a sliding selector set toward wash.}}


4. Set the CYCLE SELECTOR KNOB to WASH-RINSE. (In case drain pump 'WASH')<PIC:Manual39_6>
{{image description: Cycle Selector diagrams. One knob shows WASH-RINSE and DRAIN positions; another boxed version shows WASH, RINSE, and DRAIN positions.}}


5. Fill water in the washtub and add the detergent.<PIC:Manual39_7>
{{image description: Cartoon washing machine receiving detergent or laundry into the top opening, with a smiling washer face.}}


6. Load laundry in the wash tub and fill water to 'H' high water level.<PIC:Manual39_8>
{{image description: Line drawing of the wash tub being filled from a water tap or hose, with clothing visible inside the tub.}}


7. Set the WASH TIMER 1-15 minutes. WASH TIMER<PIC:Manual39_9>
{{image description: Wash Timer knob diagram labeled WASH TIMER with scale marks 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, and 15 and a clockwise arrow.}}


8. After washing, set the CYCLE SELECTOR KNOB to 'DRAIN' for drain.<PIC:Manual39_10>
{{image description: Cycle Selector knob set to DRAIN, with the DRAIN label on the right and CYCLE SELECTOR text below.}}


### SPIN DRY


1. Transfer the clothes into the spin basket and arrange the clothes evenly.<PIC:Manual39_11>
{{image description: Top-view spin basket illustration showing a hand placing or arranging laundry evenly inside the spin dryer basket.}}


2. Be sure to attach the safety cover and close the inner lid.<PIC:Manual39_12>
{{image description: Spin dryer basket diagram with labels inner lid and safety cover. A circular safety cover is shown being placed over laundry, and an arrow points downward inside the basket.}}


3. Close the spin dryer lid<PIC:Manual39_13>
{{image description: Spin dryer lid diagram showing a hand closing the lid downward over the spin basket.}}


4. Set the SPIN DRY TIMER 1-5 minutes. (1-10 minutes)

Caption: Standard spin dry timer knob (1-5 minutes).<PIC:Manual39_14>
{{image description: Spin Dry Timer knob diagram with scale marks 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 and a clockwise arrow.}}
Caption: Optional spin dry timer knob (1-10 minutes, Super/Delicate/Normal).<PIC:Manual39_15>
{{image description: Spin Dry Timer diagram labeled option, with settings Super 10, 7, 5 Normal, 3 Delicate, and 0 around the knob.}}


### RINSING


1. Set the CYCLE SELECTOR KNOB to WASH-RINSE. (In case drain pump 'WASH')<PIC:Manual39_16>
{{image description: Cycle Selector diagrams for rinse operation. One shows WASH-RINSE and DRAIN, and another boxed selector shows WASH, RINSE, and DRAIN.}}


2. Supply the proper amount of water as not to overflow the top of the washing tub. 3. Set the WASH TIMER 2~3 minutes.<PIC:Manual39_17>
{{image description: Wash Timer knob diagram set near 3 minutes, with scale marks 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, and 15 and a clockwise arrow.}}


4. Drain the water. Set the CYCLE SELECTOR KNOB to 'DRAIN'<PIC:Manual39_18>
{{image description: Cycle Selector knob diagram set to DRAIN, with CYCLE SELECTOR text below.}}

5. Repeat this cycle until drain water is clean. (2~3 cycles)

### OVERFLOW RINSE
1. Keep supplying water Adjust water pressure to ensure that the amount of water supplied does not exceed that water drained.
<PIC:Manual39_19>
{{image description: Two Cycle Selector diagrams labeled without pump and with pump. The without-pump selector points to WASH-RINSE, while the with-pump selector has WASH, RINSE, and DRAIN positions and points toward RINSE.}}



2. Set the WASH TIMER 6~8 minutes.<PIC:Manual39_20>
{{image description: Wash Timer knob diagram set around 6 minutes, with scale marks 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, and 15 and a clockwise arrow.}}


3. As soon as the WASH TIMER shuts off, turn off the water tap.<PIC:Manual39_21>
{{image description: Wash Timer diagram with knob set at 0 beside a water tap icon, indicating shutting off water when the timer stops.}}


4. Set the CYCLE SELECTOR KNOB to 'DRAIN'.<PIC:Manual39_22>
{{image description: Cycle Selector knob diagram set to DRAIN, with DRAIN label on the right and CYCLE SELECTOR text below.}}


### ADDITIONAL RINSE
<PIC:Manual39_23>
{{image description: Additional rinse procedure panel with six numbered steps. It shows selecting the course, setting water selector to spin and cycle selector to drain, supplying water for about 1 minute, stopping water and moving laundry with safety cover, closing the spin dryer lid, and setting spin dry timer 2-3 minutes.}}

